<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Georg II Fuchs von Dornheim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1586–1633</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Georg II Fuchs von Dornheim was prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamberg">Bamberg</a> from 1623 to 1633, known as the 'witch bishop'. Under his rule the Bamberg witch trials of 1626 to 1631 sent several hundred people to their deaths, among them the city's mayor Johannes Junius. He fled before the Swedish army in 1632 and died the following year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-georg-ii-fuchs-von-dornheim.jpg" alt="Johann Georg II Fuchs von Dornheim" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Salver, Hofkupferstecher in Würzburg (*1670 +1738) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_Georg_Fuchs_von_Dornheim.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
